00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:42.620
Was the divorce of Jim's parents a setup for the Michael-Helene relationship in season
吉姆父母的离婚是为了给第六季中迈克尔和海琳的关系做铺垫吗？

294
00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:43.200
six?
海琳是帕姆的妈妈，各位。

295
00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.760
Helene is Pam's mom, everyone.
不是。

296
00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:46.820
No.
这只是为了展现我们的剧集除了喜剧元素外，还有戏剧性时刻。

297
00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:55.560
This was crafted as a small representation of how our show had dramatic moments in addition
但因为这一集是在超级碗之后播出的，我们想避开现有的故事情节。

298
00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:56.600
to comedic ones.
所以编剧们必须创造一种全新的戏剧冲突，但又不能让它

299
00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:02.400
But because this aired after the Super Bowl, we wanted to stay away from existing storylines.
发展得太远。

300
00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:08.600
So the writers had to create kind of like a brand new drama, but one that wouldn't go
（注：原文第49条对应原句末尾，此处补全语境）

301
00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.160
on to affect our regular characters too directly.
进而直接影响到我们的常规角色。

302
00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:16.580
We didn't want anything in this episode to actually affect the character arcs and relationships
我们不想让这一集里的任何内容真正影响到

303
00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.780
that were set in place.
既定的人物弧光和人物关系。

304
00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:18.260
Yes.
是的。

305
00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.940
So that was kind of why this storyline was crafted.
所以这就是为什么这个故事情节是这样设计的。

306
00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:28.060
And I remember John and I really fighting for the drama of this.
我记得约翰和我当时真的在为这段剧情的戏剧性据理力争。

307
00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.620
Like really saying, no, we want to play this real.
就像是坚持说，不，我们想把它演得真实一点。

308
00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.240
Pam is really upset.
帕姆真的很心烦。

309
00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.180
This isn't funny upset.
这不是那种搞笑的心烦。

310
00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:42.140
Like I remember when I was shooting a three-camera show, I was supposed to get mad at one of the
我记得我拍三机位剧集的时候，我本该对其中一个

