00:32:55.990 --> 00:32:58.010
Well, we would always get really excited.
嗯，我们总是会感到非常兴奋。

807
00:32:58.370 --> 00:33:03.770
And James told us that for him, the day on set was really fun, exciting.
詹姆斯告诉我们，对他来说，在片场的那一天真的很有趣，很令人兴奋。

808
00:33:04.090 --> 00:33:07.330
I mean, he'd worked for a long time in the entertainment industry.
我是说，他在娱乐行业工作了很长时间。

809
00:33:07.630 --> 00:33:11.950
But he said when you're in front of the camera and other people are depending on you to hit
但他表示，当你站在镜头前，而其他人都在指望你站对位置、

810
00:33:11.950 --> 00:33:16.450
your mark and deliver your dialogue, all of a sudden, he got really nervous.
说好台词时，他突然感到非常紧张。

811
00:33:17.210 --> 00:33:22.110
And he said he was expecting a little more directing because he's not an actor at all.
他说他本以为导演会多给些指导，因为他根本不是演员。

812
00:33:22.310 --> 00:33:24.030
But they didn't really give him much.
但他们其实没给他太多指导。

813
00:33:24.170 --> 00:33:25.110
They're just like, go there.
他们只是说，去那儿。

814
00:33:25.530 --> 00:33:26.390
Say your line.
说你的台词。

815
00:33:26.670 --> 00:33:31.390
But he did say after one or two takes, Jeff Blitz suggested to him, maybe look like you're
但他确实说，拍了一两次之后，杰夫·布里茨建议他，或许可以表现得像在密谋什么，

816
00:33:31.390 --> 00:33:33.930
up to something, you know, give it a little something.
你知道，稍微加点戏。

817
00:33:34.490 --> 00:33:36.750
And he's like, I think that's the take they used.
他说他觉得最后用的就是那一版镜头。

818
00:33:37.310 --> 00:33:40.570
But his whole family saw it because it was on after the Super Bowl.
他的全家人都看到了，因为那集是在超级碗之后播出的。

819
00:33:40.890 --> 00:33:41.290
Yes.
是的。

820
00:33:41.490 --> 00:33:44.630
But James said when they first said, we've got a role for you.
但詹姆斯说，当他们最初告诉他，我们有个角色给你时。

821
00:33:44.770 --> 00:33:46.150
It's one line as a delivery man.
是一个送货员的台词。

822
00:33:46.290 --> 00:33:49.910
He didn't realize it was for the stress relief episode.
他当时没意识到那是《压力缓解》那一集。

823
00:33:50.070 --> 00:33:50.230
Yeah.
是啊。

824
00:33:50.450 --> 00:33:54.990
So when he said yes, he just wasn't putting it together that he was saying yes to the
所以当他答应的时候，他根本没把这事和

825
00:33:54.990 --> 00:33:56.150
Super Bowl episode.
超级碗那一集联系起来。

826
00:33:56.250 --> 00:33:58.510
He said his dad was particularly excited.
他说他父亲特别兴奋。

827
00:33:59.710 --> 00:34:03.970
And when he told his brother and sister at first, he said he thinks they didn't believe
当他起初告诉他兄弟姐妹时，他说他觉得他们根本不相信

828
00:34:03.970 --> 00:34:04.130
him.
他。

829
00:34:04.210 --> 00:34:04.990
They thought he was kidding.
他们以为他在开玩笑。

830
00:34:05.070 --> 00:34:05.270
Yeah.
是啊。

831
00:34:05.390 --> 00:34:05.470
Yeah.
是啊。

832
00:34:05.510 --> 00:34:06.550
He said they were like, yeah, sure.
他说他们当时说，行行行。

833
00:34:06.630 --> 00:34:07.190
You're going to be on.
你要上电视了。

834
00:34:07.290 --> 00:34:07.730
Yeah, whatever.
是啊，随便吧。

835
00:34:08.170 --> 00:34:09.650
And then there he was.
然后他就真的出现在那儿了。

836
00:34:09.850 --> 00:34:10.730
He was on it.
他真的出镜了。

837
00:34:10.730 --> 00:34:14.790
Well, the episode is wrapping up and so is the movie, Mrs. Albert Hannity.
好了，这一集快结束了，电影《阿尔伯特·汉尼提夫人》也快结束了。

838
00:34:15.350 --> 00:34:16.530
Andy's moved to tears.
安迪感动得热泪盈眶。

839
00:34:16.770 --> 00:34:19.970
He's watching Jack Black and Cloris Leachman break up.
他正在看杰克·布莱克和克萝丽丝·利奇曼分手。

840
00:34:20.210 --> 00:34:26.570
Yeah, she's very slowly moving up the staircase in her special motorized chair.
没错，她正坐在特制的电动椅上，非常缓慢地向上移动。

841
00:34:26.710 --> 00:34:28.510
And he's crying saying, hit reverse.
他哭着喊道，倒回去。

842
00:34:29.050 --> 00:34:34.390
So I shared last week that we shot this on location at a house in West Los Angeles.
我上周分享过，我们是在西洛杉矶的一处房子里实地拍摄的。

843
00:34:35.210 --> 00:34:39.850
Randy told me the house already had this chairlift.
兰迪告诉我，那房子里本来就有这个升降椅。

844
00:34:40.150 --> 00:34:41.810
We did not install it.
不是我们安装的。

845
00:34:42.030 --> 00:34:45.270
I would think that they scouted a house with a chairlift.
我觉得他们应该是专门找了一处有升降椅的房子。

846
00:34:45.550 --> 00:34:52.410
He also said that because they wanted this mini film to really look like a real movie,
他还说，因为他们想让这部微电影看起来真的像一部真正的电影，

847
00:34:52.730 --> 00:34:56.430
we shot the Mrs. Hannity sequence on film.
所以我们用胶片拍摄了汉尼提夫人的片段。

848
00:34:56.670 --> 00:34:57.330
Dang.
哇。

849
00:34:57.650 --> 00:35:01.350
It was our first time shooting something for our show on film.
这是我们第一次为我们的节目使用胶片拍摄。

850
00:35:01.350 --> 00:35:03.970
We normally used the digital cameras.
我们平时都是用数字摄像机的。

851
00:35:04.390 --> 00:35:07.990
We even had a Steadicam film camera.
我们甚至用了一台斯坦尼康电影摄影机。

852
00:35:08.570 --> 00:35:11.890
And since they only had one day to shoot all these scenes,
而且因为他们只有一天时间来拍摄所有这些场景，

853
00:35:12.510 --> 00:35:16.830
Jeff Blitz and Randall Einhorn did a full blocking rehearsal with stand-ins
杰夫·布里茨和兰德尔·艾因霍恩用替身进行了完整的走位排练，

854
00:35:16.830 --> 00:35:19.730
where they planned out every single shot.
他们规划好了每一个镜头。

855
00:35:19.850 --> 00:35:23.630
They created official storyboards just like you do on a film.
他们制作了正式的分镜脚本，就像拍电影时那样。

856
00:35:23.910 --> 00:35:25.890
And Randy even sent us pictures.
兰迪甚至给我们发了照片。

857
00:35:26.330 --> 00:35:26.570
Yeah.
没错。

858
00:35:26.750 --> 00:35:28.990
And they exactly match the mini movie.
它们和那部微电影完全吻合。

859
00:35:29.530 --> 00:35:32.190
There's a woman who's standing in for Cloris Leachman,
有一个替克洛里斯·利奇曼的女人，

860
00:35:32.190 --> 00:35:34.370
kind of slowly moving up the staircase.
正慢慢地走上楼梯。

861
00:35:34.650 --> 00:35:39.530
And that is how they were able to get this elaborate shoot done on film,
这就是他们能够用胶片完成这次复杂拍摄的原因，

862
00:35:39.690 --> 00:35:42.410
which normally takes a lot longer than shooting on digital.
这通常比用数字摄影机拍摄要花更长的时间。

863
00:35:42.690 --> 00:35:43.910
They could do it in one day.
他们一天就能搞定。

864
00:35:44.250 --> 00:35:44.470
Yes.
是的。

865
00:35:44.590 --> 00:35:46.810
So Randy sent us pictures of how they staged it.
所以兰迪给我们发了他们如何布置场景的照片。

866
00:35:46.870 --> 00:35:50.190
And it was so fun to see them because Anna, who was in charge of locations,
看到这些照片真有意思，因为负责外景的安娜，

867
00:35:50.610 --> 00:35:51.490
played Jack Black.
扮演了杰克·布莱克。

868
00:35:51.730 --> 00:35:51.910
Yes.
没错。

869
00:35:51.990 --> 00:35:55.170
And then Jasmine, who was our second AD, plays Cloris Leachman.
然后我们的第二副导演贾斯敏扮演了克洛里斯·利奇曼。

870
00:35:55.170 --> 00:35:58.530
So we'll have to put one of those pictures in our stories.
所以我们得把其中一张照片放到我们的故事里。

871
00:35:58.890 --> 00:36:00.110
It was fun to see their faces.
看到他们的表情真好玩。

872
00:36:00.850 --> 00:36:05.370
In addition to wrapping up the movie storyline,
除了结束电影的情节线，

873
00:36:05.930 --> 00:36:10.330
we're going to find out what exactly Jim said to Pam's dad.
我们还要弄清楚吉姆到底对帕姆的爸爸说了什么。

874
00:36:10.650 --> 00:36:10.970
Yeah.
没错。

875
00:36:11.190 --> 00:36:14.930
Pam's dad comes to the office and they have this whole conversation in the parking lot.
帕姆的爸爸来到办公室，他们在停车场进行了那场谈话。

876
00:36:15.090 --> 00:36:16.130
Now we can't hear it.
我们听不到谈话内容。

877
00:36:16.230 --> 00:36:17.990
We see it, but we don't know what they're saying.
我们能看到画面，但不知道他们在说什么。

878
00:36:18.190 --> 00:36:20.370
We had a fan question from Stephanie P.
我们收到了粉丝斯蒂芬妮·P的提问。

879
00:36:20.370 --> 00:36:23.430
What did Pam say to her dad in the parking lot?
帕姆在停车场对她爸爸说了什么？

880
00:36:23.730 --> 00:36:26.770
There was never any dialogue for this in the script.
剧本里从来没有这段对话。

881
00:36:27.110 --> 00:36:30.210
This was always a silent spy shot.
这始终是一个无声的偷拍镜头。

882
00:36:30.530 --> 00:36:32.410
In fact, here's what it said.
事实上，剧本上是这样写的。

883
00:36:32.670 --> 00:36:37.090
It said, Jim's POV, Pam is talking with her father.
上面写着：吉姆视角，帕姆正在和她父亲交谈。

884
00:36:37.390 --> 00:36:39.450
The conversation goes back and forth.
谈话来来回回。

885
00:36:39.950 --> 00:36:40.950
Pam looks angry.
帕姆看起来很生气。

886
00:36:41.330 --> 00:36:42.710
The dad says something.
爸爸说了些什么。

887
00:36:43.130 --> 00:36:45.390
She looks up at Jim with tears in her eyes.
她含着泪看向吉姆。

888
00:36:45.550 --> 00:36:48.150
The dad leaves and Pam walks back inside.
爸爸离开了，帕姆走回室内。

889
00:36:48.150 --> 00:36:51.070
So you guys just had to fill in the blanks there.
所以你们当时只能自己填补空白了。

890
00:36:51.250 --> 00:36:51.910
We did.
没错。

891
00:36:52.390 --> 00:36:55.230
Now, Pam's dad was played by Rick Overton,
帕姆的爸爸是由里克·奥弗顿饰演的，

892
00:36:55.390 --> 00:36:58.130
and he will be back again in Niagara.
他之后还会出现在《尼亚加拉》那一集里。

893
00:36:58.770 --> 00:37:01.050
And Rick is actually a really funny guy.
里克其实是个非常有趣的人。

894
00:37:01.210 --> 00:37:03.850
He's like an improvisation comedy veteran.
他是即兴喜剧的老手了。

895
00:37:04.210 --> 00:37:05.370
He's also a writer.
他也是一位编剧。

896
00:37:05.550 --> 00:37:08.510
He won an Emmy for writing an episode of Dennis Miller Live.
他曾凭借《丹尼斯·米勒直播秀》的一集剧本赢得了艾美奖。

897
00:37:09.010 --> 00:37:13.610
So it's funny to me how we would cast people with great pedigree
所以我觉得很有趣，我们竟然会找来背景如此深厚的人，

898
00:37:13.610 --> 00:37:18.070
to stand and do a silent POV shot in the parking lot.
只是为了站在停车场拍一个无声的视角镜头。

899
00:37:18.270 --> 00:37:22.070
But that was because this is a big role, Pam's dad.
但那是因为帕姆的爸爸这个角色很重要。

900
00:37:22.450 --> 00:37:27.010
If we bring him back, we need to make sure this person has the chops to go the distance.
如果我们让他回归，我们需要确保这个人有足够的实力去支撑后续的剧情。

901
00:37:27.150 --> 00:37:27.290
Yeah.
没错。

902
00:37:27.870 --> 00:37:29.130
And Rick was great.
而且瑞克表现得非常棒。

903
00:37:29.330 --> 00:37:31.290
And we just improvised dialogue.
我们当时只是即兴发挥了台词。

904
00:37:31.290 --> 00:37:37.330
We just improvised what he might be saying to her that would cause her to be hurt.
我们即兴创作了他可能会对她说的话，导致她受到伤害。

905
00:37:37.510 --> 00:37:41.410
It was mostly a spin on, like, I'm sorry, but I need to leave your mother.
内容大多是围绕着“我很抱歉，但我得离开你母亲”之类的说法。

906
00:37:41.750 --> 00:37:47.670
You know, he knew that scripted line that Pam says later, and he would say that to me,
你知道，他知道帕姆后来会说那句剧本台词，他就会对我那样说，

907
00:37:47.690 --> 00:37:50.330
